				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608067262" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1390193112 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Jan 2014 04:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1940478">
									

<p>For those who are wondering&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;number&nbsp;arrangements</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The items in twos are good things, and references &quot;double happiness&quot;. Sometimes product names include pairs of characters.<br />
The items in threes are indicative of three stages of life, and three is lucky for life.<br />
The items in fives represent the five elements of earth, water, metal, fire, and wood, which are associated with the number five.<br />
The items in eights represent wealth. And eight is generally a very lucky number in Chinese numerology.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers&nbsp;for&nbsp;overall&nbsp;backstory</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The man involved essentially found a way to lengthen his life through the use of numbers and careful arrangements. However, the messages in reddish-brown paint indicate that it wasn't a simple process.</p>
<p>My personal take? The disappearances were part of the ritual or whatever the man developed to keep himself &quot;alive&quot; as a consciousness. &quot;To let numbers become your life is to let your life become numbers.&quot; The man lives through the numbers painted on the walls in blood, which appear when he doesn't assume his usual human-looking form.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

